#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kverbos; helps learning Spanish verb conjugation. In contrast to the old 1."
"x version it isn't necessary for the user to capture verb data before "
"learning. &kverbos; comes with a set of more than 9 000 verbs and the "
"corresponding conjugation patterns. This does not mean that the program can "
"answer every question about Spanish verbs now. It is not the result of "
"linguistic research. Its purpose is to support persons learning Spanish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main purpose is to learn the verb forms. &kverbos; selects one of the "
"verbs and a time, the user enters the different forms of the verb and the "
"program tells if the solutions are correct. Graphic is used to give a "
"feedback to the user. The user can select the verbs and times that he wants "
"to practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kverbos; can be used to look up unknown verb forms, too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since KDE4 verbs can be trained in sentences, too. Also other grammar "
"exercises with gaps are possible. The program comes without such exercises "
"but it is possible to download such exercises. Look for information about "
"installing exercises in chapter 5 and about creating exercises in chapter 4."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with &kverbos;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kverbos; you will see the menu window first. In the tree "
"view you can select the exercise you want to do. A double click on a menu "
"entry is one possibility to select and start an exercise. At the bottom of "
"the window you have five round buttons to control the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menu-Windows of &kverbos;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your first step using the program should be to select verbs and tenses. Use "
"the <guiicon> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"button_config_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>Config button</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> </guiicon> "
"config-button to open the configuration dialog. In the section verbs you can "
"select verbs and in the section tenses the tenses you want to practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "The function of the buttons in detail are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guiicon><inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"button_config_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>The Config button which opens the configuration dialog</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject></guiicon>Configure &kverbos; Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens the configure dialog for &kverbos;. There you can select verbs, "
"tenses, image files for the jigsaw feedback and KVTML files where the "
"program looks for translations of verbs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guiicon><inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref="
"\"button_help_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>The Help button which gives access to some help options.</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject></guiicon>The Help Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First the button reveals three more buttons. One leads to the handbook, one "
"offers short information about &kverbos; and the last general information "
"about &kde; itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guiicon><inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"button_next_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>The Next button which starts the next step in the program</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject></guiicon>Next Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Next Button has different functions. Let the mouse hover above the "
"button and you will see what it actually does. It starts the next action in "
"the program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guiicon><inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"button_menu_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>The Config button which opens the configuration dialog</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject></guiicon>Menu Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are learning and you press the Menu-button you will be brought back "
"to the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guiicon><inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"button_quit_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> "
"<phrase>The Config button which opens the configuration dialog</phrase> </"
"textobject> </inlinemediaobject></guiicon>Quit Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "As the name tells you leave the program with this button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kverbos; trainer windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the selected exercise you will see different windows. There is "
"a window where you can enter an infinitive of a verb and the program will "
"show you how to conjugate the verb. Another type of exercise selects tense "
"and infinitive and you enter the forms. Or you select a gap exercise. The "
"last type of exercises does not come with the program. You have to install "
"additional files to get them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "The VerbViewTrainer - Look up verb forms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Have a look at the <emphasis>\"VerbViewTrainer-\"</emphasis> window. Here "
"you can look up how to conjugate the verb that you have entered in the input "
"line. Every infinitive you enter is counted as an exercise. If it exists in "
"the programs database it is counted as a correct solution too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "The VerbViewTrainer Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot VerbViewTrainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "The FormsTrainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have to be more active in the <emphasis>\"FormsTrainer-\"</emphasis> "
"window. &kverbos; selects a verb and a tense. You have to enter the forms "
"into the lineedit fields. After that you can use the <guiicon> "
"<inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"button_next_kl.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Config button</phrase> "
"</textobject> </inlinemediaobject> </guiicon> Next-button to correct your "
"input. If some of your entered forms are not correct the color is changed to "
"red. You have a second chance to find the solution. If you have no idea you "
"can go to the solution with the <guiicon> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"button_next_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Config button</phrase> </textobject> </"
"inlinemediaobject> </guiicon> Next-button. With this button you can cycle "
"through the whole process: enter forms, correct the input, show the "
"solution, go to the next verb."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "The FormsTrainer Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot FormsTrainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The GapTrainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another type of trainer window is the <emphasis>\"GapTrainer-\"</emphasis>. "
"You can practice verb conjugation in sentences. Read the task, enter the "
"forms into the gaps and use the <guiicon> <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject> "
"<imagedata fileref=\"button_next_kl.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase>Config button</phrase> </textobject> </"
"inlinemediaobject> </guiicon> Next-button to go through the correction cycle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will not see this kind of trainer in a &kverbos; standard installation. "
"To use this trainer you need additional exercise files. Have a look at the "
"&kverbos; webpage to find such files. If exercise files are installed the "
"program extends the menu with this exercises. For further information read "
"the chapter for <link linkend=\"developers\">developers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "The GapTrainer Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot GapTrainer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to configure &kverbos;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Dialog: General"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "The General Configuration Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot General Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show buttons for the Spanish characters ñ, á, é, í, ó, ú"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the setup of your keyboard it might not be possible to enter "
"the above mentioned characters. This option helps you. If it is selected, a "
"line of button with the characters is shown below the trainer window. You "
"can insert ñ, á, é, í, ó, ú with these buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use a verb selection instead the entire verb stock"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As &kverbos; comes with over 9 000 verbs and you might not know all of them "
"you can select verbs and practice this selection. With this option you "
"decide if your selection is used or all the verbs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select verbs automatically if they aren't in the selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes there are verbs in an exercise that you still did not select. This "
"may happen in the VerbViewTrainer or the GapTrainer. If you have selected "
"this option the program adds new verbs to your selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore accent while checking the user input"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Although it is clear that accents belong to correct spelling the user can "
"check this option and the accents will be ignored during the correction "
"process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "The use of the clock"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left side of the trainer window there is a clock. It can be used in "
"two ways. It simply counts the time that you are learning until all "
"exercises are done or you finish your learning process or it works as a "
"counter. That means you select a time and the clock counts backwards until "
"this time has expired. So you can learn a fixed time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Dialog: Tenses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Tenses Configuration Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot Tenses Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select Tenses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the tenses you can learn are listed here. Select the ones you want to "
"practice. This selection affects the FormsTrainer. It only uses tenses that "
"you have selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "Proportion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We talk of normal tense in this part if the tense is formed only by one "
"word. Composed tenses have a form of haber or estar as the first part "
"followed by the particip or a gerund. Because haber and estar are always "
"conjugated the same way the composed tenses are considered easier and they "
"should not ask as often as the normal tenses. You can set the proportion "
"here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Dialog: Verbs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Verbs Configuration Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:376 index.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot Verbs Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can see a tab-widget with three tabs that helps you to select and "
"deselect the verbs you want to train."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "First Tab: List of selected Verbs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All selected verbs are listed here. These verbs will be used for training. "
"If this list is empty you cannot start studying and the program will give "
"you a hint to select verbs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "Second Tab: Verbs in Grammatical groups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The known verbs grouped by different conjugation patterns. This helps you to "
"select verbs of a special type, &eg; irregular verbs or changing verbs where "
"'e' becomes 'ie' like 'querer' (group verbs e --> ie)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "Third Tab: Verbs in Alphabetical Groups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "As the name of the tabs says the verbs or sorted alphabetical."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We mustn't forget the input line below the tab widget. Here you can enter a "
"word or a part of word and the programs looks for infinitives that match "
"your input."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You cannot add new verbs to the list or delete one from the list. You cannot "
"edit the verbdata, too. If you encounter mistakes in the verb data, write an "
"e-mail to the author."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Dialog: KVTML-Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "The KVTML-Files Configuration Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot KVTML-Files Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The verb database doesn't contain any translations of the Spanish "
"infinitives. If you like to work with translations into other languages you "
"can use your favorite KVTML-files containing the translations. You can add "
"several files here. The program reads the files and searches for verbs and "
"their translations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid "List of KVTML-files to load"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of files that you have already selected. You can add and delete files "
"here. These files are used to search for translations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translated Verbs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjust how the translated words are used in &kverbos;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Dialog: Jigsaw"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Jigsaw Configuration Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can decide if you want to make use of the jigsaw view. Its purpose is to "
"give some motivation. Select images that are used as pictures for the "
"jigsaw. You can also define how many pieces should be made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Developer's Guide to &kverbos;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kverbos; can be extended with gap exercises. This chapter informs you how "
"to create exercises and how to install them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "Install exercise files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The exercise files can be installed for the whole system or for the user "
"only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation for the whole system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to install exercises so that they are available for every user "
"you have to put the files into the '$KDEDIR/share/kde4/apps/kverbos/"
"exercises/' folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation for a user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you install the exercise files into the folder '$HOME/.kde4/share/apps/"
"kverbos/exercises/' only this user can see and use them. This way users can "
"add additional exercises by themselves."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create additional exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every exercise consists of at least three files: 'exercisename.html', "
"'exercisename.menu.en', 'exercisename.solution'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "The 'exercisename.html' file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the exercise itself as it will be presented to the &kverbos; user in "
"the program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "The 'exercisename.menu.en' file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The file contains information used to extend the menu in the program. The "
"menu will be extended, so that the user can select the exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "The 'exercisename.solution' file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the solution. It is used by the program to evaluate the "
"user input."
msgstr ""

